course: dictionary
lesson: 14182
title: Words from a country: Mongolian
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where something comes from. Mongolian is one of these. It can describe a thing, as in «The Mongolian herders moved their animals across the steppe.» Here it tells you which herders: the ones from Mongolia.
explain: The same word can name a person or a language. «Batbold is a Mongolian who lives in Ulaanbaatar.» Here Mongolian means a person from Mongolia. «Ali is learning Mongolian at school.» Here it means the language spoken there.
explain: To know which meaning is right, look at the words around it. Is it describing a thing, naming a person, or naming a language? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If it makes sense, you have it.
fact: Mongolian means from or to do with Mongolia, a country between Russia and China.
fact: A Mongolian is a person from Mongolia. The plural is Mongolians.
fact: Mongolian is also the name of the language spoken in Mongolia.
fact: Long ago, Genghis Khan led the Mongol Empire, and its people were famous riders on the wide steppe.
fact: «A ger», also called a yurt, is a round home used by many Mongolian nomads.
exercise: «The Mongolian herders moved their animals across the steppe.» What does Mongolian tell us about the herders? | They are all called Khan | They live by the sea | *They come from Mongolia | They speak in a whisper
exercise: «Ali is learning Mongolian at school.» What does Mongolian mean here? | A person from Mongolia | A wide grassy plain | *The language spoken in Mongolia | A round tent
exercise: «Batbold is a Mongolian who lives in Ulaanbaatar.» What is Batbold? | A river in Russia | The name of a language | *A person from Mongolia | A country between Russia and China
test: «The Mongolian family lived in a ger on the steppe.» What is a ger? | A large river | *A round home, also called a yurt | A kind of language | A person from Mongolia
test: Which one is a Mongolian? | A wide grassy plain | A country between Russia and China | The language of Mongolia | *A person from Mongolia
exam: «Her grandmother was born in Mongolia, and she speaks Mongolian.» What does Mongolian mean in this sentence? | *The language spoken in Mongolia | A person from Mongolia | Something from the steppe | A round tent
